%TC=3.                               Areas Menu Help.
%TC=7.
At this menu you can choose to either...
%TC=6.
%TC=7.[R] REDISPLAY%TC=6. Message areas and their settings.
%TC=7.[+] ALL-ON%TC=6.  Switches all message areas to ON status.
%TC=7.[-] ALL-OFF%TC=6. Switches all message areas to OFF status.
%TC=7.[#] BUNDLE%TC=6. Bundle Menu.
%TC=7.[M] MODE%TC=6. Edit options Mode.
%TC=7.[S] SAVE-AREAS%TC=6. Allows you to save Areas ON/OFF settings.
%TC=7.[!] QUIT%TC=6. Exit QWK bundler and return back to the BBS.

%TC=7.
 REDISPLAY:
%TC=6.
This will show again a full list of the message areas you have access to.
And their current status. You should check these areas and make sure that
their settings are what you require. Most importantly, check whether their
status is ON or OFF. This decides whether messages in this area will be
used in the Bundle packet you can generate for download.
%TC=7.
 ALL-ON: Message area status.
%TC=6.
This sets the Area status setting for ALL the areas to ON.
Typically you would select this option when you want to bundle messages
from ALL the available areas. (You can then fine tune your selection by
then switching OFF a few areas if not required, by using 'MODE' menu
option - See below.)
%TC=7.
 ALL-OFF: Message area status.
%TC=6.
This sets the Area status setting for ALL the areas to OFF.
Typically you would select this option when you want to bundle messages
from only a few of the available areas. (You can then fine tune your
selection by then switching ON a few areas if required, by using 'MODE'
menu option - See below.)
%TC=7.
 BUNDLE: Bundle menu.
%TC=6.
When the message Areas and their pointers/status suit your requirements,
you should select this menu option to goto the Bundle menu. There you can
select to Download the messages you have marked.
%TC=7.
 MODE: Message areas pointers.
%TC=6.
This is the most critical option in this menu. On choosing this command you
can then fine-tune a message areas pointers and status.
By selecting 'MODE' you can toggle between 3 Edit option.
 eg. 1. On/Off.
        This MODE allows you to select an individual message area
        (By cursoring to it OR pressing its number 0-9)
        If you cursor to the area you want, you can then press return
        and the area will toggle ON or OFF as desired.
        If you simply press the Areas number it will automatically toggle
        ON/OFF as desired without pressing return.

     2. Edit Start Number.
        This MODE allows you to select an Area as described above, you can
        then enter a start number to bundle from. The default is your 'Last
        read' pointer and most times you will have no need to select this
        option.

     3. Grab number from Area.
        This allows you to choose a maximum number of messages to grab from
        an Area. You select the Area as already described above. You can then
        enter the number you desire. The default is to grab as many messages
        as possible that are considered 'unread' according to your 'last read'
        pointer for the Area. Most times you will have no need for this
        option and will use the defaults.


%TC=7.
 SAVE AREAS: Allows you to save Areas ON/OFF settings.
%TC=6.
It can be a nuisance toggling on/off the same areas each time you want to use
the QWK bundler. For this reason you can save off a record of the Areas you
want by choosing this option. NOTE: Any currently edited Areas option in the
QWK will be lost. So only select this option at the start of a session!

%TC=7.
 QUIT: Back to BBS.
%TC=6.
If you want to abandon the QWK bundler and return to the BBS then choose
this option.
%TC=7.
